  "body": "## Issue\nLOT-120\nCloses #211\nClaim: cloud/lot-120-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5\n\n## What and why\nProblem: the Plus entries \"Crédits\" and \"Charte du forum\" showed a placeholder, and Réglages had no Maintenance or À propos section.\n\nChange (spec: `docs/lots/LOT-120-maintenance-about.md`, legacy reference `87fe0d1c`):\n- **About** (Plus > Crédits): version and build, the two HFR+ topics ([TU] Super HFR+, Beta) by id form, opened in the reader through LOT-095's router (`ReaderTarget(link:)`), never Safari; \"Nouveautés\" (changelog) and \"Crédits\".\n- **Static pages**: credits (reproduces CREDITS.md and the licence) and the forum charter (legacy text unchanged), bundled HTML in a `WKWebView` with page JavaScript off; links go through the browser rule.\n- **Réglages**: \"Maintenance\" (system-settings shortcut, with an empty `cacheRows` slot for LOT-179) and \"À propos\" (version).\n- **Changelog source**: `tooling/docs/export-app-changelog.py` exports the \"Résumé (FR)\" column of `CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` to `App/SwiftHFR/Resources/changelog-v1.json` (`--check` reports a stale copy; not in CI yet).\n- Not built, on purpose: cache sizes (LOT-179, #419), cache clearing (LOT-187, #689). \"Aide\" is not ported (not reachable in legacy SwiftUI): decision reported to the orchestrator.\n\n## How it was verified\nCloud session: the app cannot be built here, so the CI is the first build. SwiftLint `--strict` clean on the changed folders. Swift Testing, shown to fail without the change as they test new types or new routing (not run locally): `AboutModelTests` (version, the two exact URLs, topic routes of category 25, reader per link), `StaticPageTests` (pages bundled, no script, credits links/names/licence against CREDITS.md and LICENSE, link actions, a real `WKWebView` that does not run a page script), `ChangelogTests`, `MaintenanceModelTests`, `RootModelTests` (credits and charter built). `check-lot-deps.py` and `export-app-changelog.py --check` pass.\n\n## Mac checks\n- [ ] iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0): Plus > Crédits shows About; both topic rows open the reader in the app, back returns to About.\n- [ ] Logged out and logged in: both topics open (Apple category hidden, Q-7); #298 is captured (`R298a`-`R298f`: 301 then 200, logged out and in); the #329 comment is drafted, not posted yet.\n- [ ] Credits and charter pages: light, dark, Dynamic Type XL, iPad sidebar entry; a tapped credits link opens Safari's view (or the system browser when \"Navigateur par défaut\" is on).\n- [ ] Réglages > Maintenance \"Ouvrir les réglages système\" opens the app's page in Settings; À propos shows `version (build)`.\n- [ ] The bundled resources land in the app bundle root (`static-credits.html`, `static-charter.html`, `static-page.css`, `changelog-v1.json`) with the synchronized group.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (App only)\n- [x] Tests added/updated\n- [x] No secrets; no fixture, no pseudo\n- [x] Docs updated (lot spec, App/README, tooling/docs/README)\n- [x] Author model: Sonnet 5.5 / Reviewer model: Opus (must differ)\n- [x] Ledger: one `changelog` entry below, label `ledger`\n\n### Ledger\n\n```changelog\n| UX | Crédits : les liens vers les sujets [TU] Super HFR+ et bêta s'ouvrent dans l'app (lecteur), par identifiants, et non dans Safari. | LOT-120 #718 | `credits.html:12` @ `87fe0d1c`, capture R298e |\n```\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHLNjxSFxhva1KwRyZ\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
