   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/lot-120-review-opus, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 838d0da\n\n1. **Medium**, `docs/lots/LOT-120-maintenance-about.md:57,62` and the PR's Mac checks. The spec still treats #298 as a *pending capture*. #298 is closed, its captures `R298a`-`R298f` merged in #554, and `HFR-PROTOCOL.md:553-559` records both id forms as 301 then 200, logged out and logged in alike. Because of that the acceptance criterion (\"links open logged out, as #298 shows\") cites nothing (L03, L12, L17), and the comment the issue requires on review #329 was never posted. Fix: cite `R298a`-`R298d` for the URLs and the logged-out case, drop \"pending\", and post the #329 comment.\n2. **Low**, spec, Intentional differences: \"Links are never handed to `appDelegate.openURL` (it does not exist)\" is false. It exists at `Classes/HFRplusAppDelegate.m:764-777` @ 87fe0d1c: it opens the default browser when `open_links_in_default_browser` is on, otherwise `SFSafariViewController`. That is exactly what `StaticPage.action` does, so this is parity, not a difference. The cited `StaticInfoPageView.swift:165-169` is the `#Preview`; the link handling is at `:126-137`. The spec also names `StaticPageModel.action`, but the code has `StaticPage.action`.\n3. **Low**, the `### Ledger` entry: \"le legacy gardait un slug périmé\" presents the stale slug as a defect. `R298e`/`R298f` show HFR answers it with a 301 to the current page. The real change is \"opened in the app, not in Safari\". Reword the entry and cite `R298e`.\n4. **Low**, `AboutView.swift:62-64` and `Resources/changelog-v1.json`. `Text(entry.summary)` with a `String` does not render Markdown, so row 40 shows `**vous**` literally. Several rows also show internal references to users (`R05a`, `§7b B2`, `#278`, `md_passs`). Fix: strip or render the Markdown in the export script, and decide whether the internal references stay.\n5. **Low**, `AboutView.swift:44-47` and `PlusView.swift:52` (L49). The `NavigationLink` destinations are built eagerly, so every body evaluation decodes the changelog JSON and reads the HTML and CSS from disk. Fix: load once, in `.task` or a cached static.\n6. **Nit**, `StaticPageTests.swift:97`. The test expects `evaluateJavaScript` to return JS `null`, which bridges badly with the non-optional async overload. Return a string instead (e.g. `String(document.body.getAttribute('data-ran'))`).\n\n**Checked**\n- SwiftLint `--strict`: clean on the changed folders.\n- `check-lot-deps.py`, `export-app-changelog.py --check` and `ledger.py check-body`: all pass.\n- `HFRLinkRoute` probe: both URLs route to topic, category 25, posts 1711 and 8811, page 1.\n- The URLs equal the operator's comment on #211.\n- The charter body is byte-identical to legacy `charte.html`.\n- All 8 links from CREDITS.md and the licence files appear as `href` in the credits page.\n- Swift 6 isolation probe (`@MainActor` closures, `replacing(maxReplacements:)`) compiles.\n- API signatures match the existing code. Flat resources, no name clash, no project file edit.\n- No secrets.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
