   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/lot-120-review-opus, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 09280fa\n\n1. **High**, `StaticPageView.swift:24-27`. While `html` is nil, the `Group` has no child, and SwiftUI applies a `Group`'s modifiers to its children. So `.task` may never fire: html stays nil and Crédits and Charte show a blank page, maybe without a title. Fix: render a placeholder in the else branch (`ProgressView()` or `Color.clear`), or move `.task` to a view that is always there. `ChangelogView` is fine, because its `.task` sits on the `List`.\n2. **Nit**, `LOT-120-maintenance-about.md:57`. The spec says \"Review #329 got a comment saying so\", but the comment is only drafted (the PR says so). Post it or reword the line.\n3. **Nit**, finding 4 is half done. The `**` marks are stripped, but internal references (`R05a`, `§7b B2`, `#278`) still reach users, and no decision on them is recorded.\n\nFindings 2, 3, 5 (`ChangelogView`) and 6 are resolved. Finding 1 is resolved apart from the #329 wording (Nit 2 above).\n\n**Checked**: the commit diff. `changelog-v1.json` equals what the new script exports and has no `*` left. The PR body's ledger entry and Mac checks are updated. The test change is sound (`String(null)` gives `\"null\"`).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
